        "metadata": {
            "kira_final": "Done. `/app/run.py` contains `run_tasks(tasks, max_concurrent)` (importable via `from run import run_tasks`), using only the standard library.\n\nHow it works:\n- A semaphore bounds concurrency to `max_concurrent`; each task is wrapped in a coroutine and run with `asyncio.gather`.\n- **KeyboardInterrupt safety:** when running in the main thread, it installs a SIGINT handler that cancels the internal gather instead of letting the loop die. On cancellation it cancels all still-running worker tasks and awaits them (`return_exceptions=True`), so their `finally` blocks / context-manager cleanup fully execute — then raises `KeyboardInterrupt` so your own `try/except KeyboardInterrupt` still works. The original signal handler is restored afterwards.\n\nVerified by tests:\n1. 20 tasks with limit 4 → all complete, peak concurrency exactly ≤ 4.\n2. Cancellation mid-run → every started task's cleanup ran.\n3. Real `SIGINT` to a subprocess → cleanup printed for running tasks, then \"caught KI\" and normal exit.",
            "session_id": "tb-60f26bf903"
        }
